#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""grabd: D-Bus service that records application audio streams.

Bus name org.grab.Recorder, object /org/grab/Recorder, interface org.grab.Recorder1

  ListItems()            -> a(sa{sv})  items in display order (id, properties)
  ListInputs()           -> a(ssb)     microphones: (name, description, is_default)
  Toggle(s id)                          available -> recording -> paused -> recording ...
  SetInput(s id, s input)               "" none, "default" follow default mic, or source name
  Remove(s id, b with_data)             remove a finished item (done / empty / failed);
                                        with_data also moves its files to the Trash
  RemoveFinished(b with_data)           Remove() every finished item
  SaveNow(s id)                         save an MP3 snapshot of a recording/paused item now
  RemoveRecord(s id)                    discard a recording/paused item's recording: stop it,
                                        move its MP3 and FLAC to the Trash; the stream is
                                        offered again
  signal ItemsChanged(a(sa{sv}))        full item list after any change
  signal InputsChanged(a(ssb))          full input list after any change
  GetState()             -> s          JSON {"items": [{properties}], "inputs":
                                        [{"name", "description", "default"}], "folder"}
  signal StateChanged(s)                GetState() after any change (for clients
                                        that handle JSON more easily than variants)

Item properties: id, title, app, state, busy, pending, stream, input,
input_description, file, duration, error.
  state:   available | recording | paused | encoding | done | empty | failed
  busy:    an MP3 snapshot/final encode is queued or running for this item
  pending: a Toggle is in progress (starting, pausing or resuming); further
           Toggles are ignored until it is done
  error:   why the last start failed (state stays available), or for
           finished items what went wrong

Recording: one hidden 4-channel virtual null sink per recording; the app stream
is linked (alongside its normal routing) into its first two channels and the
chosen input into the other two. One ffmpeg captures it as a single stream
("Grab: <title>" in volume controls), splits the channels, gates the input's
background noise, mixes both and writes a lossless FLAC with silence removed.
If the input's source goes away or changes (mic unplugged and replugged, new
default), it is relinked. Pause unlinks and saves an MP3
snapshot; resume relinks and appends. When the stream disappears the item is
finalized (state encoding -> done/empty/failed) and stays until removed.
Encodes are serialized in one background queue and coalesced per item.

Metadata lives in the files' tags (ID3 in the MP3, Vorbis comments in the
FLAC): title, date (start time), and grab=1 (the marker), grab_app,
grab_input. MP3s in the recordings folder that carry the marker and belong to
no item (earlier sessions) are listed as done items; others are not listed.
Removing a finished item strips the marker (a lossless copy of the MP3) and
keeps the MP3; removing it with data moves the MP3 and any leftover FLAC to
the Trash (restoring them brings the item back). Items disappear when their
MP3 is deleted or loses the marker.

Requires: python-dbus-next, ffmpeg, pipewire-pulse (pactl), pipewire (pw-link, pw-dump).
Optional: python-mutagen (reads tags and removes the marker in place, in
milliseconds; without it ffprobe reads tags and ffmpeg copies the file).
"""
